One common source of vulnerabilities in Java web applications is the improper handling of user input when interacting with the operating system, which can lead to Command Injection.

```java
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.InputStreamReader;

public class CommandInjectionExample {
    public void executePing(String ipAddress) {
        try {
            // This line is vulnerable because it concatenates raw user input 
            // directly into a system command string without validation.
            // An attacker could input "8.8.8.8 ; rm -rf /" to execute malicious commands.
            String command = "ping -c 4 " + ipAddress;

            Process process = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command);

            // Read the output...
            BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(process.getInputStream()));
            String line;
            while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                System.out.println(line);
            }
        } catch (Exception e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```

